{
  "name": "srm_bench_small",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "PROVISIONAL - small switched reluctance machine (SRM) bench pack, 3-phase / 6-tooth rotor with a bench CV source (96 V, 60 A). The analytic flux-map SRM shares the machine-family chain: knee-distorting bridge, current halls + fault points, phase-ADC view, truth power diagnostics (Hypot reads |I_U|+|I_V| as the loss-law magnitude input - SRM windings are not a dq pair; the v2 PMSM-bridge loss constants are extrapolated here and are a calibration target. Shaft semantics: Dyno/FreeInertia Poles=1, mechanical rad/s end to end (an SRM has no synchronous frame). Encoder parametrized mechanically as well (Poles=1).",
